cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Mitochondrial toxicity prediction from molecular structure:
  a QSAR classifier for mitochondrial membrane potential disruption
message: If you use this software or its curated dataset, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Saha
    given-names: Asmita
abstract: >-
  A gradient-boosted QSAR classifier for mitochondrial membrane potential
  disruption, trained on 5,938 compounds curated from the Tox21 qHTS screen
  (PubChem AID 720637) and evaluated once on a frozen, analogue-disjoint test
  set of 1,205 compounds (PR-AUC 0.709, ROC-AUC 0.926). The repository
  documents the curation decisions in full, including a provenance analysis
  showing that 93% of the MitoTox database's membrane-potential records derive
  from a single Tox21 follow-up study and therefore do not constitute an
  independent data source.
keywords:
  - QSAR
  - cheminformatics
  - computational toxicology
  - mitochondrial toxicity
  - Tox21
  - food additives
  - RDKit
  - machine learning
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-21"
